<title>UNITED NATIONS: Kofi Annan will be seventh U.N. secretary-general.</title>
<headline>Kofi Annan will be seventh U.N. secretary-general.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kofi Annan of Ghana, who takes office on Jan. 1, 1997, will be the seventh United Nations secretary-general since the world body was founded more than 50 years ago.</p>
<p>Previous secretaries-general were: Boutros Boutros-Ghali of Egypt (1992-1996) Javier Perez de Cuellar of Peru (1982-1991) Kurt Waldheim of Austria (1972-1981) U Thant of Burma (1961-1971) Dag Hammarskjoeld of Sweden (1953-1961, when he was killed in an air crash in Africa) Trygve Lie of Norway (1946-1953)</p>
</text>
